                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "48731ae5-fee7-4009-90be-81111d925c22",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4136928-2db9-3981-b75a-e86077b5bee9",
                        "source_sense_id": "c64467c1-3549-321e-b8db-ccb366662fcd",
                        "target_lang_word": "coquetry",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "coquetry",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "37bcd48c-2e2d-3157-8aad-090a5331396e",
                                        "entry_id": "3eb53b35-51d7-3dd0-807e-360c9571b2f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Coquettish behaviour; actions designed to excite erotic attention, without intending to reciprocate such feelings (chiefly of women towards men); flirtatious teasing."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "15eade24-48e7-41eb-ad0f-9ac6aacc8f71",
                                                "sense_id": "37bcd48c-2e2d-3157-8aad-090a5331396e",
                                                "text": "With a lover […] her sensibility will naturally lead her to endeavour to excite emotion, not to gratify her vanity, but her heart. This I do not allow to be coquetry, it is the artless impulse of nature […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2dc86928-cef0-35f5-9e47-b3d83c09d51f",
                                        "entry_id": "3eb53b35-51d7-3dd0-807e-360c9571b2f9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An act constituting such behaviour; an affectation of amorous interest or enticement, especially of a woman directed towards a man."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f29e62a9-c7fc-46e1-b962-b5db9d1f6cbc",
                                                "sense_id": "2dc86928-cef0-35f5-9e47-b3d83c09d51f",
                                                "text": "The little coquetries, which are as natural to a gay young girl as her laughter, were all in full play, and had she gone no further no harm would have been done."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3d87862b-e9a2-44a3-87ab-ea6dd84710d9",
                                                "sense_id": "2dc86928-cef0-35f5-9e47-b3d83c09d51f",
                                                "text": "The mischievous pleasure of her coquetries was forgotten, and in a rush of glad confidence she felt a woman's pride in him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a5603ee3-1465-496a-9828-5968d0750a56",
                                                "sense_id": "2dc86928-cef0-35f5-9e47-b3d83c09d51f",
                                                "text": "\"Her pretty little coquetries are like the gambols of a kitten."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7c402807-8db0-42a9-9885-da707a6e8c9d",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4136928-2db9-3981-b75a-e86077b5bee9",
                        "source_sense_id": "c64467c1-3549-321e-b8db-ccb366662fcd",
                        "target_lang_word": "coquetería",
                        "target_lang_code": "es",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "coquetería",
                                "target_lang_code": "es",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f70a6283-8cb6-353a-bd65-57c738d8e661",
                                        "entry_id": "f6f23bf7-6829-3e5d-b71b-f0a3489532d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Acción o efecto de coquetear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4cec176-d0c5-35d7-9a10-b577760a0852",
                                        "entry_id": "f6f23bf7-6829-3e5d-b71b-f0a3489532d2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Modo de actuar que busca atraer la atención romántica o sexual de alguien, especialmente en el cuidado de los modales y la apariencia personal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"2\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "ad521e1d-4141-45bb-8e53-212cf8461f45",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4136928-2db9-3981-b75a-e86077b5bee9",
                        "source_sense_id": "c64467c1-3549-321e-b8db-ccb366662fcd",
                        "target_lang_word": "Koketterie",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Koketterie",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f4adbe67-8988-30cf-9954-9174a7933c21",
                                        "entry_id": "ff016289-7a52-39c6-8ef1-bde6eafc50a1",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "das Verhalten einer Person, die einer Person des anderen Geschlechts gefallen möchte"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d69d8e6-a67a-4662-a685-870e3bc921b2",
                                                "sense_id": "f4adbe67-8988-30cf-9954-9174a7933c21",
                                                "text": "„Sie schien Koketterie für unerläßlich zu halten und zierte sich wie eine späte Jungfrau.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5b2a0f9-8415-4db5-946e-037bda3ee1d6",
                                                "sense_id": "f4adbe67-8988-30cf-9954-9174a7933c21",
                                                "text": "„Er besang eine Frau, die Herrscherin über sein Herz, die ihn allmählich umbringe mit ihrer Koketterie.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ff55443-0e09-4f9c-80ca-159c1a886398",
                                                "sense_id": "f4adbe67-8988-30cf-9954-9174a7933c21",
                                                "text": "„Von Koketterie war sie ganz frei und brauchte hierin ihrer Natur gar nicht erst Gewalt anzutun.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c34a2cd8-99d9-48e3-a696-be2685443cfa",
                                                "sense_id": "f4adbe67-8988-30cf-9954-9174a7933c21",
                                                "text": "„Diese Einstellung entspricht der Natur des weiblichen Geschlechts und ist der einzige Grund für die Koketterie, die man einer Frau mit Recht verzeiht, während man sie einem Mann nie verzeihen könnte.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "9785e977-90b3-40b8-9fc0-b5f9e8e01fbe",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4136928-2db9-3981-b75a-e86077b5bee9",
                        "source_sense_id": "c64467c1-3549-321e-b8db-ccb366662fcd",
                        "target_lang_word": "кокетство",
                        "target_lang_code": "ru",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "кокетство",
                                "target_lang_code": "ru",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5721d271-c4cf-34d5-a158-05a32e34ad86",
                                        "entry_id": "0bad5dad-01c8-3378-b9a8-254abfb4524a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "поведение того, кто стремится понравиться, привлечь внимание; кокетничает (обычно — применительно к женщине)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c57d589a-d68a-4aad-a9b7-ad3b9f926ca6",
                                                "sense_id": "5721d271-c4cf-34d5-a158-05a32e34ad86",
                                                "text": "Своей женственной грацией, стройностью, хорошеньким, свежим лицом и шаловливым кокетством она привлекала сердца."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e14c20b3-78e4-4c7a-90cd-737e9142c5f3",
                        "source_entry_id": "c4136928-2db9-3981-b75a-e86077b5bee9",
                        "source_sense_id": "46f8ec2f-1aaa-3a78-9e7c-a0bd76e0494e",
                        "target_lang_word": "Gefallsucht",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Gefallsucht",
